  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes Holafly Different</h2>
  <p>
    Holafly sells unlimited data instead of a fixed GB bucket. That's the whole pitch: no counting gigabytes, no panic when a video call runs long. It's why Holafly usually costs more per day than a GB-capped competitor for a short trip, but can work out cheaper if you're a heavy data user or bad at rationing a data cap. If you'd rather pay by the gigabyte and use less, a provider like <a href="/airalo/">Airalo</a> is probably the better fit.
  </p>
  <p>
    One thing worth knowing about the code itself: <strong>ADAMANDLINDS</strong> is one of the only codes that covers both Holafly product lines &mdash; 5% off a one-off destination eSIM and 10% off a monthly Plans subscription. Most codes floating around only do one of the two (a code good on a destination eSIM usually won't apply to a Plans subscription, and vice versa), so it's worth checking which product a code you find elsewhere actually covers before you assume it'll work at checkout.
  </p>

